WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:17.402
Coby: Did you think of an idea for the science fair yet?

2
00:00:17.403 --> 00:00:20.513
Mark: Yep. I'm going to watch a plant.

3
00:00:20.514 --> 00:00:22.346
To see how it grows.

4
00:00:22.347 --> 00:00:25.681
Coby: You're going to watch a plant?

5
00:00:25.682 --> 00:00:28.688
Mark: It'll be cool.

6
00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:34.621
Coby: It sounds . . . um . . . boring.

7
00:00:34.622 --> 00:00:37.403
Mark: Really?

8
00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:42.027
Coby: Yeah. But I'm glad you're not making a tornado in a bottle.

9
00:00:42.028 --> 00:00:52.522
Coby: Everybody is making those!

10
00:00:52.523 --> 00:00:54.371
Mark: Come on, plant.

11
00:00:54.372 --> 00:01:04.249
Don't just sit there. Grow!

12
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.420
Zack: You look weird.

13
00:01:06.421 --> 00:01:07.917
What are you doing?

14
00:01:07.918 --> 00:01:10.324
Mark: I'm working on my science project.

15
00:01:10.325 --> 00:01:13.238
Mark: It was fun when the seed sprouted.

16
00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.165
Mark: But now it's—

17
00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:24.092
Zack: Boring!

18
00:01:24.093 --> 00:01:29.117
Juan: Hi, Mark. Want to come out and play football?

19
00:01:29.118 --> 00:01:32.580
Mark: I can't. I'm working on my project.

20
00:01:32.581 --> 00:01:34.562
Mark: I'm watching a plant grow.

21
00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:54.025
Juan: Oh. That sounds . . . uh . . . fun! Bye.

22
00:01:54.026 --> 00:01:55.968
Mark: Coby and Zack were right.

23
00:01:55.969 --> 00:02:03.880
This project is boring!

24
00:02:03.881 --> 00:02:13.669
Mark: Hey, guys! Can I play football?

25
00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:17.679
Coby: When are we going to share our science projects?

26
00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.475
Miss Gray: The fair is still weeks away, Coby.

27
00:02:20.476 --> 00:02:23.218
Miss Gray: We'll share them on the day of the fair.

28
00:02:23.219 --> 00:02:25.096
Maya and Jenna: I can't wait!

29
00:02:25.097 --> 00:02:27.947
Kara: My project is sooo great!

30
00:02:27.948 --> 00:02:31.809
Kara: I'm going to win a ribbon for sure!

31
00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.242
Miss Gray: I'm sure everyone will have a great project.

32
00:02:35.243 --> 00:02:39.505
Miss Gray: I'm looking forward to . . .

33
00:02:39.506 --> 00:02:42.269
Miss Gray: Mark? What's wrong?

34
00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:47.882
Mark: I have a problem—a science fair problem!
